    "https://schreiner.edu/job/student-assistant-office-support/": {
      "title": "Student Assistant",
      "description": "Student Assistant – Office Support - Schreiner University Skip to content Request Information Anonymous Reporting Toggle Navigation Library Calendar Map Visit Canvas Schreiner One IT Support Academy Prep Shop Toggle Navigation Admissions Academics Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni News Search Apply Now Toggle Navigation Admissions Academic Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni Visit Us Apply Now Shop Schreiner Quick Links News Library Event Calendar Campus Map Schreiner One Canvas Student Assistant – Office Support Student Kerrville Texas Posted 3 days ago Website schreineru Schreiner University Position Title: Student Assistant – Office Support Department : Mental Health Services Reports To: Director of Wellness and Mental Health Services SUMMARY OF RESPONSIBILITIES The Mental Health Services Student Assistant for Office Support will provide administrative and logistical support for Mental Health Services. This position will help maintain an organized, welcoming, and functional space for students to utilize to rest, recharge, and conduct private virtual counseling sessions through Timely Care. The student assistant will help monitor and maintain designated private rooms used by students for virtual appointments, assist with the organization and preparation of the space, and provide general administrative support to Claire Arnold, the Director of Wellness and Mental Health Services. This position does not provide mental health treatment or advice to students. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Provide a kind, welcoming, and professional presence at the front desk for students visiting the Mental Health Services suite. Help maintain and organize the Mental Health Services suite, including designated private rooms used by students for virtual counseling appointments through Timely Care. Monitor use of the virtual-care rooms and help ensure spaces are clean, orderly, private, and ready for student use. Help organize office supplies, informational materials, and resources within the Mental Health Services suite. Prepare rooms and materials for student use and wellness programming. Help identify and communicate basic maintenance requests or technology concerns with the appropriate campus office. Assist with maintaining informational displays, brochures, flyers, and other wellness related materials. Create and post social media content for Mental Health Services Assist the Director with administrative projects, organization, data entry, and other administrative tasks as needed. Maintain appropriate privacy and discretion when working in a mental health services environment. Refer students seeking counseling, crisis support, or other clinical assistance to the Director, Timely Care, or the appropriate professional or campus resource rather than attempting to provide support independently. Perform other duties related to student wellness and mental health services as assigned. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE AND SKILLS REQUIRED Current Schreiner University undergraduate student eligible for work-study employment. Strong people skills. Dependable, responsible, and able to work independently. Strong organizational and communication skills. Comfortable interacting professionally with students, faculty, and staff. Able to maintain appropriate privacy and discretion. Comfortable learning basic office and technology systems. Interest in student wellness, mental health, health promotion, or supporting the college community is preferred. Proficiency in Canva is preferred DESIRED QUALITIES Creative and energetic Organized and dependable Friendly and approachable Maintain appropriate privacy and discretion when working in a mental health services environment Strong communicator Comfortable taking initiative Team-oriented Interested in improving the student experience IMPORTANT BOUNDARIES OF THE POSITION This is a non-clinical student support position. The student employee will not provide counseling, crisis intervention, mental health assessments, clinical advice, or other mental health services. Student employees will receive guidance regarding appropriate boundaries, privacy, and procedures for directing students to professional resources. TO APPLY Send resume and cover letter to mcarnold@schreiner.edu Apply for Job Schreiner University 2100 Memorial Blvd Kerrville, TX 78028 Directions | 830.896.5411 Financial Services | 830.792.7303 FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions | 830.792.7217 admissions@schreiner.edu Office Hours: 8am – 5pm, Mon -Fri Prospective Students Request Information Apply Financial Services Transcript Requests FAQ Consumer Information Directory About Visitors Donor Alumni Careers at Schreiner Graduate Assistantship Campus Map Schreiner Experiences Box Office Library & Textbooks Schreiner Technology Schreiner Retail Store Community Supporters SU2030 Strategic Plan Security Title IX Privacy Policy CARES Act and HEERF © Schreiner University | 2100 Memorial Blvd. Kerrville, TX 78028-5611 – 830.896.5411 Financial Services: 830.792.7303 – FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions: 830.792.7217 – admissions@schreiner.edu ANONYMOUS REPORTING Campus Conduct Hotline: 866-943-5787 Page load link Search Schreiner Resources Academic Programs Financial Services University Directory Students | Faculty | Staff Schreiner One Canvas Pounce This site uses cookies and other third-party services. For more information please see our Privacy Policy . Accept & Close Go to Top"
    },
    "https://schreiner.edu/job/student-assistant-wellness-programming/": {
      "title": "Student Assistant",
      "description": "Student Assistant – Wellness Programming - Schreiner University Skip to content Request Information Anonymous Reporting Toggle Navigation Library Calendar Map Visit Canvas Schreiner One IT Support Academy Prep Shop Toggle Navigation Admissions Academics Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni News Search Apply Now Toggle Navigation Admissions Academic Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni Visit Us Apply Now Shop Schreiner Quick Links News Library Event Calendar Campus Map Schreiner One Canvas Student Assistant – Wellness Programming Student Kerrville Texas Posted 3 days ago Website schreineru Schreiner University Position Title: Student Assistant – Wellness Programming Department : Mental Health Services Reports To: Director of Wellness and Mental Health Services SUMMARY OF RESPONSIBILITIES The Mental Health Services Student Assistant for Wellness Programming & Events will support the development and implementation of wellness and mental health programming for Schreiner University students. Working closely with Claire Arnold, the Director of Wellness and Mental Health Services, this position will assist with planning campus events, connecting with campus partners, promoting wellness initiatives, and creating engaging opportunities for students to learn about and participate in mental health and wellness activities. This position is ideal for a student who enjoys event planning, creativity, communication, and helping build a positive and supportive campus community. This position does not provide mental health treatment or advice to students. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Assist with planning and coordinating wellness and mental health events and programs on campus. Help brainstorm engaging programming based on student interests and campus needs. Assist with communicating and coordinating with campus partners, student organizations, faculty, staff, and community organizations as directed. Help contact campus partners and coordinate logistics for events. Assist with scheduling spaces, gathering supplies, preparing materials, and coordinating event details. Help with event setup, registration, welcoming participants, and cleanup. Assist with creating and distributing promotional materials, flyers, social media content, and other outreach materials in coordination with appropriate campus offices. Help maintain calendars and planning documents for wellness programming. Create and post social media content for Mental Health Services Assist with collecting informal feedback from students about programs and events. Help organize wellness resources and materials for distribution to students. Assist the Director with special projects related to student wellness, mental health awareness, prevention, and campus engagement. Perform other duties related to wellness programming as assigned. Refer students seeking counseling, crisis support, or other clinical assistance to the Director, Timely Care, or the appropriate professional or campus resource rather than attempting to provide support independently. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE AND SKILLS REQUIRED Current Schreiner University undergraduate student eligible for work-study employment Strong communication and interpersonal skills Organized and able to manage multiple tasks and deadlines Strong people skills Comfortable communicating with faculty, staff, students, and campus/community partners Creative and enthusiastic about developing student programming Comfortable working independently and collaborating with a team Experience with event planning, social media, graphic design, marketing, or student organizations is preferred but not required Interest in mental health, wellness, health promotion, or student engagement is preferred. Proficiency in Canva is preferred DESIRED QUALITIES Creative and energetic Organized and dependable Friendly and approachable Maintain appropriate privacy and discretion when working in a mental health services environment Strong communicator Comfortable taking initiative Team-oriented Interested in improving the student experience IMPORTANT BOUNDARIES OF THE POSITION This is a non-clinical student support position. The student employee will not provide counseling, crisis intervention, mental health assessments, clinical advice, or other mental health services. Student employees will receive guidance regarding appropriate boundaries, privacy, and procedures for directing students to professional resources. TO APPLY Send resume and cover letter to mcarnold@schreiner.edu Apply for Job Schreiner University 2100 Memorial Blvd Kerrville, TX 78028 Directions | 830.896.5411 Financial Services | 830.792.7303 FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions | 830.792.7217 admissions@schreiner.edu Office Hours: 8am – 5pm, Mon -Fri Prospective Students Request Information Apply Financial Services Transcript Requests FAQ Consumer Information Directory About Visitors Donor Alumni Careers at Schreiner Graduate Assistantship Campus Map Schreiner Experiences Box Office Library & Textbooks Schreiner Technology Schreiner Retail Store Community Supporters SU2030 Strategic Plan Security Title IX Privacy Policy CARES Act and HEERF © Schreiner University | 2100 Memorial Blvd. Kerrville, TX 78028-5611 – 830.896.5411 Financial Services: 830.792.7303 – FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions: 830.792.7217 – admissions@schreiner.edu ANONYMOUS REPORTING Campus Conduct Hotline: 866-943-5787 Page load link Search Schreiner Resources Academic Programs Financial Services University Directory Students | Faculty | Staff Schreiner One Canvas Pounce This site uses cookies and other third-party services. For more information please see our Privacy Policy . Accept & Close Go to Top"
    },
    "https://schreiner.edu/job/nursing-instructor-vocational-nursing/": {
      "title": "Nursing Instructor-Vocational Nursing",
      "description": "Nursing Instructor-Vocational Nursing - Schreiner University Skip to content Request Information Anonymous Reporting Toggle Navigation Library Calendar Map Visit Canvas Schreiner One IT Support Academy Prep Shop Toggle Navigation Admissions Academics Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni News Search Apply Now Toggle Navigation Admissions Academic Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni Visit Us Apply Now Shop Schreiner Quick Links News Library Event Calendar Campus Map Schreiner One Canvas Nursing Instructor-Vocational Nursing Full Time Kerrville Texas Posted 1 week ago Website schreineru Schreiner University Nursing Instructor-Vocational Nursing SUMMARY OF RESPONSIBILITIES Provides academic and clinical instruction within the Department of Nursing. Plans, coordinates, and conducts classroom and/or clinical experiences for students. Reports directly to the Director of Undergraduate Nursing. Responsibilities also include a strong commitment to advising, student progression, and retention. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Maintains academic standards as established by the nursing department and Teaches students in clinical, laboratory, and classroom settings as Participates in planning, organization, and deployment of courses as appropriate to assignment. Participates in the development, implementation, and evaluation of course activities as appropriate to Participates in program and department activities associated with professional Incorporates new knowledge and techniques in clinical, classroom, and laboratory Maintains working knowledge of technology required to perform Displays a scholarly orientation to the assumption of the responsibilities of a full-time university faculty member: Utilizes teaching-learning principles Serves as a knowledgeable resource person to students and Shares professional expertise at the local Understands and follows both Schreiner University and Division of Nursing faculty and student handbooks. Responds to emails and other forms of communication promptly throughout the work. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE AND SKILLS REQUIRED Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) is preferred. Minimum of a Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) required for vocational nursing instruction. Unencumbered license to practice professional nursing in Texas or another interstate compact state. Current American Heart Association BLS certification. Up-to-date immunizations and other compliance requirements as per Division of Nursing Faculty Handbook. At least 3 years of hands-on clinical experience 1 year of nursing education experience preferred. Effective organizational, interpersonal, verbal, and written communication that promotes teamwork and student engagement. Working Conditions Generally, works in climate-controlled environments, sitting, standing, stooping, walking, bending, pushing and/or pulling and reaching. Uses computer equipment. Requires manual dexterity and both hands to perform nursing functions. Lifting up to 50 pounds may be required. Apply for Job Schreiner University 2100 Memorial Blvd Kerrville, TX 78028 Directions | 830.896.5411 Financial Services | 830.792.7303 FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions | 830.792.7217 admissions@schreiner.edu Office Hours: 8am – 5pm, Mon -Fri Prospective Students Request Information Apply Financial Services Transcript Requests FAQ Consumer Information Directory About Visitors Donor Alumni Careers at Schreiner Graduate Assistantship Campus Map Schreiner Experiences Box Office Library & Textbooks Schreiner Technology Schreiner Retail Store Community Supporters SU2030 Strategic Plan Security Title IX Privacy Policy CARES Act and HEERF © Schreiner University | 2100 Memorial Blvd. Kerrville, TX 78028-5611 – 830.896.5411 Financial Services: 830.792.7303 – FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions: 830.792.7217 – admissions@schreiner.edu ANONYMOUS REPORTING Campus Conduct Hotline: 866-943-5787 Page load link Search Schreiner Resources Academic Programs Financial Services University Directory Students | Faculty | Staff Schreiner One Canvas Pounce This site uses cookies and other third-party services. For more information please see our Privacy Policy . Accept & Close Go to Top"
    },
    "https://schreiner.edu/job/administrative-specialist-for-the-center-for-talent-and-workforce-development/": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist for the Center for Talent and Workforce Development",
      "description": "Administrative Specialist for the Center for Talent and Workforce Development - Schreiner University Skip to content Request Information Anonymous Reporting Toggle Navigation Library Calendar Map Visit Canvas Schreiner One IT Support Academy Prep Shop Toggle Navigation Admissions Academics Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni News Search Apply Now Toggle Navigation Admissions Academic Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni Visit Us Apply Now Shop Schreiner Quick Links News Library Event Calendar Campus Map Schreiner One Canvas Administrative Specialist for the Center for Talent and Workforce Development Full Time Kerrville Texas Posted 3 weeks ago Website schreineru Schreiner University Administrative Specialist for the Center for Talent and Workforce Development SUMMARY OF RESPONSIBILITIES Under the guidance of the Director of the CTWD, the Administrative Specialist plays a crucial role contributing to the effective operational functioning and excellent student experience of the Center. This individual is responsible for the day-to-day administrative management of the CTWD, ensuring all activities align with university objectives, policies, and applicable regulations. The Administrative Specialist coordinates the director’s schedule, supports student enrollment, and oversees financial transactions (including purchase orders, check requests, and credit card reconciliations), and manages marketing and promotional operations. Serving as an organizational hub for the department, this individual must be highly organized, adept at multitasking across concurrent projects, and agile in learning and managing a variety of internal software systems. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Coordinates and maintains the Director’s calendar, arranges appointments, prepares meeting materials, and coordinates logistics (meeting spaces, technology, and catering). Fosters clear, professional communication with university leadership, academic departments, campus partners, and external stakeholders. Serves as custodian of departmental records, ensuring high standards of confidentiality, data integrity, and professional office standards. Oversees purchase orders (POs), check requests, and monthly departmental credit card statements. Coordinates and assists with the enrollment and registration processes for CTWD students and program participants. Supports event and instructional delivery, including logistics for workshops, career fairs, webinars, and online courses across platforms such as Zoom, Teams, or Google Meet. Maintains CTWD’s social media presence across platforms under the strategic direction of the Director. Oversees departmental print and digital collateral (flyers, booklets, brochures, and program guides); keeps materials stocked and organized, prepares collateral for events/career fairs, archives obsolete files, and makes timely content updates. Researches, sources, creates, orders, and maintains inventory of promotional items and branded giveaways for outreach events, conferences, and career fairs. Effectively multitasks and balances priorities across multiple simultaneous departmental initiatives. Quickly learns, navigates, and maintains proficiency across a variety of institutional platforms, software tools, and management systems. Performs other related duties as assigned. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE AND SKILLS REQUIRED High School diploma or equivalent required; some college preferred. 2+ years of administrative support, office management, or program coordination experience. Experience with basic budget oversight, purchase orders, invoicing, or credit card reconciliation. Proven experience managing social media channels (e.g., LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram) in a business or educational setting. High technological agility with a demonstrated ability to learn and adapt to multiple software platforms, databases, and administrative systems quickly. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and cloud collaboration tools. Familiarity with virtual conferencing platforms (Zoom, Microsoft Teams, Google Meet). Basic design/layout familiarity for updating promotional flyers and digital graphics (e.g., Canva or similar design tools) is a plus. Exceptional Organization & Multitasking: Demonstrated ability to manage competing deadlines, coordinate multiple active projects, and prioritize tasks effectively in a dynamic environment. Customer Focus & Communication: Strong written, interpersonal, and verbal communication skills with a student-centered approach. Discretion & Initiative: Sound judgment, proactive problem-solving ability, and adherence to strict confidentiality standards. Valid Texas driver’s license, reliable transportation, and an insurable driving record. Apply for Job Schreiner University 2100 Memorial Blvd Kerrville, TX 78028 Directions | 830.896.5411 Financial Services | 830.792.7303 FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions | 830.792.7217 admissions@schreiner.edu Office Hours: 8am – 5pm, Mon -Fri Prospective Students Request Information Apply Financial Services Transcript Requests FAQ Consumer Information Directory About Visitors Donor Alumni Careers at Schreiner Graduate Assistantship Campus Map Schreiner Experiences Box Office Library & Textbooks Schreiner Technology Schreiner Retail Store Community Supporters SU2030 Strategic Plan Security Title IX Privacy Policy CARES Act and HEERF © Schreiner University | 2100 Memorial Blvd. Kerrville, TX 78028-5611 – 830.896.5411 Financial Services: 830.792.7303 – FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions: 830.792.7217 – admissions@schreiner.edu ANONYMOUS REPORTING Campus Conduct Hotline: 866-943-5787 Page load link Search Schreiner Resources Academic Programs Financial Services University Directory Students | Faculty | Staff Schreiner One Canvas Pounce This site uses cookies and other third-party services. For more information please see our Privacy Policy . Accept & Close Go to Top"
    },
