    "https://schreiner.edu/job/assistant-director-of-the-center-for-talent-and-workforce-development/": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of the Center for Talent and Workforce Development",
      "description": "Assistant Director of the Center for Talent and Workforce Development - Schreiner University Skip to content Request Information Anonymous Reporting Toggle Navigation Library Calendar Map Visit Canvas Schreiner One IT Support Academy Prep Shop Toggle Navigation Admissions Academics Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni News Search Apply Now Toggle Navigation Admissions Academic Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni Visit Us Apply Now Shop Schreiner Quick Links News Library Event Calendar Campus Map Schreiner One Canvas Assistant Director of the Center for Talent and Workforce Development Full Time Kerrville Texas Posted 4 weeks ago Website schreineru Schreiner University Assistant Director of the Center for Talent and Workforce Development ABOUT THE CENTER FOR TALENT AND WORKFORCE DEVELOPMENT (CTWD) At the Center for Talent and Workforce Development (CTWD), we are dedicated to building a brighter future for Texas by contributing to the Schreiner 2030 Strategic Plan and Texas 2036 Strategic Framework. Our mission is to strengthen the state’s workforce, economy, and community through impactful training programs and community-focused education initiatives. Our diverse offerings are designed for anyone who is ready to start, refocus, or elevate their careers. Programs include certification programs, continuing education, professional development, workshops, webinars, and networking events. Aligned with Texas’s economic strategic goals, CTWD empowers individuals with the skills and knowledge needed to contribute meaningfully to the state’s evolving workforce, fostering both professional development and community impact. SUMMARY OF RESPONSIBILITIES The Assistant Director provides leadership and operational support for the development, promotion, and delivery of workforce and continuing education programs at CTWD. This position works closely with the Director to implement strategic initiatives, ensure program excellence, manage key external partnerships, and oversee grant and apprenticeship program administration. The Assistant Director serves as a primary point of contact for internal and external stakeholders and may supervise staff or projects as delegated by the Director. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Collaborate with the Director to develop and implement strategic plans aligned with CTWD’s mission and goals. Support budgeting, enrollment management, and marketing efforts in collaboration with the Director. Lead community outreach and relationship-building efforts with local businesses, nonprofits, and workforce organizations, and work closely with key external stakeholders to advance collaborative workforce initiatives. Supervise staff and student workers, fostering a productive and collaborative working environment. Represent CTWD at job fairs, community events, workshops, and networking events, to promote programs and generate leads. Coordinate and report on grants and apprenticeship programs with internal teams and external partners. Assist the Director with program development, implementation, and day-to-day operations. Coordinate with instructors, facilitators, and content partners to ensure the smooth delivery of the program and positive student experience. Provide student support by responding to questions, resolving concerns, and connecting them with resources. Monitor and report on program performance, enrollment, and engagement metrics to inform continuous improvement. Perform other related duties as assigned. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE AND SKILLS REQUIRED Bachelor’s degree in education, business, communications, or a related field. Minimum of 3 years of administrative or project coordination experience. Experience working in education, workforce development, or nonprofit sectors. Experience managing programs, budgets, and compliance. Proven ability to supervise and train staff effectively. Ability to solve practical problems and deal with a variety of concrete variables in situations where only limited standardization exists. Ability to interpret a variety of instructions furnished in written, oral, or diagram form. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with experience in community engagement or outreach. Detail-oriented, organized, and able to manage multiple projects simultaneously. Experience and proficiency with commonly used Internet browsers, as well as proficiency in Microsoft Outlook, Word, Excel, and Canva are required. Must be able to learn and utilize various CRMs: Jenzabar and Jenzabar Recruitment Manager. Ability to work occasional evenings or weekends for community events. Must have a valid Texas driver’s license, related insurance, and a good driving record to drive any vehicle, including personally owned vehicles, on behalf of the University. Apply for Job Schreiner University 2100 Memorial Blvd Kerrville, TX 78028 Directions | 830.896.5411 Financial Services | 830.792.7303 FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions | 830.792.7217 admissions@schreiner.edu Office Hours: 8am – 5pm, Mon -Fri Prospective Students Request Information Apply Financial Services Transcript Requests FAQ Consumer Information Directory About Visitors Donor Alumni Careers at Schreiner Graduate Assistantship Campus Map Schreiner Experiences Box Office Library & Textbooks Schreiner Technology Schreiner Retail Store Community Supporters SU2030 Strategic Plan Security Title IX Privacy Policy CARES Act and HEERF © Schreiner University | 2100 Memorial Blvd. Kerrville, TX 78028-5611 – 830.896.5411 Financial Services: 830.792.7303 – FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions: 830.792.7217 – admissions@schreiner.edu ANONYMOUS REPORTING Campus Conduct Hotline: 866-943-5787 Page load link Search Schreiner Resources Academic Programs Financial Services University Directory Students | Faculty | Staff Schreiner One Canvas Pounce This site uses cookies and other third-party services. For more information please see our Privacy Policy . Accept & Close Go to Top"
    },
    "https://schreiner.edu/job/resident-director/": {
      "title": "Resident Director",
      "description": "Resident Director - Schreiner University Skip to content Request Information Anonymous Reporting Toggle Navigation Library Calendar Map Visit Canvas Schreiner One IT Support Academy Prep Shop Toggle Navigation Admissions Academics Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni News Search Apply Now Toggle Navigation Admissions Academic Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni Visit Us Apply Now Shop Schreiner Quick Links News Library Event Calendar Campus Map Schreiner One Canvas Resident Director Part Time Kerrville Texas Posted 2 weeks ago Website schreineru Schreiner University Resident Director SUMMARY OF RESPONSIBILITIES The Resident Director (RD) is a part-time, live-in professional responsible for the daily operations and oversight of one or more residential communities at Schreiner University. The RD plays a vital role in building an inclusive and engaging living-learning environment that supports student success, community development, crisis management, and staff supervision. A successful RD demonstrates a strong commitment to student development and institutional values while fostering community engagement and maintaining building operations. The position reports to the Director of Residence Life and includes frequent evening and weekend responsibilities, on-call coverage, and engagement with students across all areas of the residential experience. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Leadership and Supervision Supervise and support a staff of Resident Assistants (RAs) and a Senior Resident Assistant (SRA). Conduct weekly staff meetings and regular one-on-one check-ins. Evaluate staff performance and support their professional development. Assist in the recruitment, selection, training, and evaluation of student staff. Support and help facilitate fall, spring, and in-service RA training sessions. Foster staff leadership through mentorship, coaching, and access to professional development opportunities. Serve as a professional liaison for students, families, and university constituents. Develop and maintain positive and productive working relationships with facility services, food service, and security personnel. Student Success & Community Engagement Implement the department’s Residential Experience through programming, intentional interactions, and leadership development initiatives. Promote a positive living-learning environment and responsible community membership. Engage students through social, cultural, recreational, and educational programming. Collaborate with campus partners on initiatives related to student retention, academic success, and well-being. Encourage faculty engagement in residence hall activities and programs. Take meals in campus dining facilities to maintain visibility and connection with residents. Crisis Management & Student Support Serve in a weekly departmental on-call rotation covering all on-campus residential communities. Conduct evening rounds during assigned on-call weekends and check in with RAs on duty. Respond to student concerns, incidents, and crises, providing appropriate support, documentation, and follow-up. Act as a student conduct officer within the assigned community. Refer students to campus resources to address academic, emotional, or social concerns. Maintain confidentiality regarding student and university matters in accordance with university policy. Building & Operational Management Oversee community operations including opening, closing, occupancy management, and maintenance. Manage room assignments, move-ins/outs, room change requests, and occupancy tracking. Collaborate with maintenance and custodial staff to ensure safe, clean, and functional living environments. Report maintenance and custodial concerns electronically in an efficient manner such that needs gain attention and problems are resolved in a timely fashion. Conduct and document routine health and fire safety inspections. Submit maintenance and custodial requests efficiently and monitor resolution timelines. Maintain administrative records related to facilities, budgets, programming, and conduct. Administrative Functions Support departmental assessments and evaluation of programs and services. Administer and maintain documentation of routine fire safety checks. Assist the Director of Residence Life in development of procedures for housing registration, hall assignments, opening and closing the residence halls, and room changes/consolidation. Assume primary responsibility for completion of these procedures within respective residence hall. Maintain high level of confidentiality regarding student, departmental, divisional, and University information and activities when appropriate. Assist the Director of Residence Life in the development of research and assessment methods to obtain data on student interests, perceptions, and needs. OTHER DUTIES Promote integration of Residence Life with academic initiatives and faculty involvement. Represent Residence Life at university events, trainings, and committee meetings. Complete other tasks, special projects, and responsibilities as assigned by the Director of Residence Life, Assistant Director, or Dean of Students. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE AND SKILLS REQUIRED Bachelor’s degree and/or some college or equivalent experience required. Master’s degree in College Student Personnel or related field preferred. Experience living in a group setting expected. Residence Life or Student Activities experience preferred. Knowledge of student and/or human development strongly desired. Exceptional organizational skills. Ability to work with minimum structure and guidance expected. Must have solid problem-solving skills. Willing and able to take initiative. Ability to facilitate multiple tasks with frequent interruptions. Supervisory experience. Ability to work weekends, evenings and on-call as required. Apply for Job Schreiner University 2100 Memorial Blvd Kerrville, TX 78028 Directions | 830.896.5411 Financial Services | 830.792.7303 FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions | 830.792.7217 admissions@schreiner.edu Office Hours: 8am – 5pm, Mon -Fri Prospective Students Request Information Apply Financial Services Transcript Requests FAQ Consumer Information Directory About Visitors Donor Alumni Careers at Schreiner Graduate Assistantship Campus Map Schreiner Experiences Box Office Library & Textbooks Schreiner Technology Schreiner Retail Store Community Supporters SU2030 Strategic Plan Security Title IX Privacy Policy CARES Act and HEERF © Schreiner University | 2100 Memorial Blvd. Kerrville, TX 78028-5611 – 830.896.5411 Financial Services: 830.792.7303 – FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions: 830.792.7217 – admissions@schreiner.edu ANONYMOUS REPORTING Campus Conduct Hotline: 866-943-5787 Page load link Search Schreiner Resources Academic Programs Financial Services University Directory Students | Faculty | Staff Schreiner One Canvas Pounce This site uses cookies and other third-party services. For more information please see our Privacy Policy . Accept & Close Go to Top"
    },
    "https://schreiner.edu/job/nursing-academic-success-coordinator/": {
      "title": "Nursing Academic Success Coordinator",
      "description": "Nursing Academic Success Coordinator - Schreiner University Skip to content Request Information Anonymous Reporting Toggle Navigation Library Calendar Map Visit Canvas Schreiner One IT Support Academy Prep Shop Toggle Navigation Admissions Academics Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni News Search Apply Now Toggle Navigation Admissions Academic Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni Visit Us Apply Now Shop Schreiner Quick Links News Library Event Calendar Campus Map Schreiner One Canvas Nursing Academic Success Coordinator Full Time Kerrville Texas Posted 3 weeks ago Website schreineru Schreiner University Nursing Academic Success Coordinator SUMMARY OF RESPONSIBILITIES The Nursing Academic Success Coordinator is a professional academic-support staff member within the Office of Academic Success who provides specialized academic support to pre-nursing and nursing students. The position combines subject-area expertise with evidence-based tutoring, academic coaching, learning strategies, and assessment preparation to help students successfully navigate their coursework/labs and prepare for progression through their academic program and, ultimately, professional licensure examinations. The position works collaboratively with faculty and nursing program leadership to support student success while maintaining clear distinctions between academic support and faculty responsibilities for course instruction, curriculum, assessment, grading, and academic progression decisions. The student population served includes all pre-nursing and nursing students in the undergraduate and vocational nursing programs: Vocational Nursing, Associate Degree in Nursing, and Bachelor of Science in Nursing. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Provides individual and small-group tutoring to pre-nursing and nursing students in nursing related coursework/labs. Maintains regular tutoring hours and provides targeted academic support to students referred by faculty or identified through established student-success processes. Develops and facilitates nursing-focused study sessions, workshops, review sessions, and other academic-support programming. Helps students develop effective study habits, time-management skills, test-taking strategies, and approaches to learning and retaining complex nursing content. Provides academic support for standardized nursing assessments and NCLEX-style examinations, including question analysis, clinical reasoning, prioritization, and test-taking strategies. Provides academic coaching and helps students develop individualized study and success plans based on their academic needs. Recruits, trains, schedules, and supervises nursing peer tutors and coordinates nursing tutoring. Maintains appropriate records of attendance to tutoring, coaching, workshops, and other academic-support activities. Refers students to appropriate campus resources, including advising, accessibility services, tutoring, Supplemental Instruction, the Writing Center, Career Services, and other Academic Excellence programs. Maintains current knowledge of nursing subject matter, evidence-based learning strategies, and current NCLEX-RN and Next Generation NCLEX testing frameworks. This position may require teaching. Performs other duties related to academic support and student success as assigned. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE AND SKILLS REQUIRED Current, unencumbered Texas or compact Registered Nurse (RN) license required Bachelor’s degree in Nursing (BSN) required; master’s degree in nursing, education, or a related field preferred. Nursing practice experience sufficient to provide subject-area expertise to pre-nursing and nursing students. Experience providing tutoring, academic support, teaching, mentoring, or related student-support services preferred. Familiarity with nursing education, standardized nursing assessments, and NCLEX-RN/Next Generation NCLEX testing preferred. Current American Heart Association Healthcare Provider BLS/CPR required; ACLS and/or PALS preferred. Strong communication, interpersonal, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively with faculty and staff. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and common educational technology. . Apply for Job Schreiner University 2100 Memorial Blvd Kerrville, TX 78028 Directions | 830.896.5411 Financial Services | 830.792.7303 FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions | 830.792.7217 admissions@schreiner.edu Office Hours: 8am – 5pm, Mon -Fri Prospective Students Request Information Apply Financial Services Transcript Requests FAQ Consumer Information Directory About Visitors Donor Alumni Careers at Schreiner Graduate Assistantship Campus Map Schreiner Experiences Box Office Library & Textbooks Schreiner Technology Schreiner Retail Store Community Supporters SU2030 Strategic Plan Security Title IX Privacy Policy CARES Act and HEERF © Schreiner University | 2100 Memorial Blvd. Kerrville, TX 78028-5611 – 830.896.5411 Financial Services: 830.792.7303 – FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions: 830.792.7217 – admissions@schreiner.edu ANONYMOUS REPORTING Campus Conduct Hotline: 866-943-5787 Page load link Search Schreiner Resources Academic Programs Financial Services University Directory Students | Faculty | Staff Schreiner One Canvas Pounce This site uses cookies and other third-party services. For more information please see our Privacy Policy . Accept & Close Go to Top"
