    "https://schreiner.edu/job/vocational-nursing-program-coordinator-and-clinical-coordinator/": {
      "title": "Vocational Nursing Program Coordinator and Clinical Coordinator",
      "description": "Vocational Nursing Program Coordinator and Clinical Coordinator - Schreiner University Skip to content Request Information Anonymous Reporting Toggle Navigation Library Calendar Map Visit Canvas Schreiner One IT Support Academy Prep Shop Toggle Navigation Admissions Academics Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni News Search Apply Now Toggle Navigation Admissions Academic Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni Visit Us Apply Now Shop Schreiner Quick Links News Library Event Calendar Campus Map Schreiner One Canvas Vocational Nursing Program Coordinator and Clinical Coordinator Full Time Kerrville Texas Posted 1 month ago Website schreineru Schreiner University Vocational Nursing Program Coordinator and Clinical Coordinator SUMMARY OF RESPONSIBILITIES This full-time, staff position reports to the Director of  Undergraduate Nursing. The position requires nursing licensure; a Bachelor of Nursing degree is preferred. A minimum of two years of teaching experience in a professional nursing program, including demonstrated knowledge, skills, and abilities in administration, is preferred. The Vocational Nursing Program Coordinator will work with the Director to coordinate curriculum, didactic and clinical courses, and facilitate clinical coordination across the continuum of undergraduate nursing programs. The Vocational Nursing Program Coordinator and Nursing Clinical Coordinator is responsible for administrative oversight and leadership of the Vocational Nursing program in collaboration with the Director of Undergraduate Nursing. This person collaborates with nursing leadership to manage the VN program. Active involvement is expected with nursing and other health care organizations at the state, regional, and national levels. Although this position is largely administrative, teaching is the University’s primary mission, and this role includes at least 6 credit hours of teaching responsibilities per year. Scholarly activity, student advising, and service to the University and community are also expected. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Represents the governing entity and the Vocational Nursing program. Fulfills the authorized role to coordinate the program in collaboration with the Director. Implements all policies and ensures that University and Nursing policies are congruent and documents any differences due to accreditation standards. Administers, manages, and evaluates the Vocational Nursing program to include curriculum, admissions, and retention. Selects appropriate clinical sites and clinical schedules across the continuum of undergraduate nursing consistent with the expectations of the Texas Board of Nursing rules for clinical learning. Collaborates with Program Directors and faculty to select and onboard clinical instructors consistent with the needs of each program and the expectations of the Texas Board of Nursing rules for clinical learning. Develops and manages Approves and implements policies for the admission, progression, probation, and dismissal of students. Collaborates and assists in recruiting and marketing of students. Ensures the enforcement of student policies. Assigns faculty to teach content in their areas of expertise and knowledge Supervises, supports, evaluates, and provides guidance to faculty. Notifies the Board of Nursing Staff immediately when there is a change in the name of the program director or in contact information. Responsible for the budgetary process that ensures the nursing program’s success. Develops and maintains an environment conducive to the teaching/learning process. Serves as a liaison for the nursing program with the administration of the governing entity. In collaboration with the VN Program Director, leads the faculty in the development, implementation, and evaluation of the curriculum All curriculum is faculty-led, developed, implemented, and evaluated. Maintains an ongoing relationship with the community and with clinical affiliating agencies. Advocates for adequate faculty to teach in the program. Ensures that the faculty/student ratios are maintained by accreditation standards. Makes budget recommendations to the VN Program Director related to faculty development and employment needs as well as program resources. Coordinate with practice Familiarize self with university mission, values, policies, and Implement the instructional, educational, and professional objectives of the Vocational Nursing Work directly with faculty, staff, and students to develop quality teaching, professional learning experiences, and public service programs. Supervise full-time, part-time, and adjunct Complete all Course Virtual Observations, Evaluations, and Analyses as required by accrediting bodies such as the Texas Board of Nursing. Refine and implement an application process to sustain and increase Collaborate and work in tandem with university partners achieving program implementation of all instructional tracks A faculty teaching load of at least 6 credit hours per year is required for this position. OTHER FUNCTIONS: Contribute to team efforts to deliver a quality nursing education program by completing assigned activities as requested and in a timely manner. Act to facilitate sustainable inter-professional relationships between faculty, students, University administrators and employees, and public or private organizations using professional communication techniques. Maintain University and professional safety. Other duties as assigned. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE AND SKILLS REQUIRED Earned Master’s in Current Texas Board of Nursing active Registered Nurse license. Experience in population-specific nursing for two years. Clinical practice in Successful teaching and administrative experience in a nursing program. Ability to work effectively with faculty and University committees and with public and private organizations both within or beyond his or her discipline. Apply for Job Schreiner University 2100 Memorial Blvd Kerrville, TX 78028 Directions | 830.896.5411 Financial Services | 830.792.7303 FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions | 830.792.7217 admissions@schreiner.edu Office Hours: 8am – 5pm, Mon -Fri Prospective Students Request Information Apply Financial Services Transcript Requests FAQ Consumer Information Directory About Visitors Donor Alumni Careers at Schreiner Graduate Assistantship Campus Map Schreiner Experiences Box Office Library & Textbooks Schreiner Technology Schreiner Retail Store Community Supporters SU2030 Strategic Plan Security Title IX Privacy Policy CARES Act and HEERF © Schreiner University | 2100 Memorial Blvd. Kerrville, TX 78028-5611 – 830.896.5411 Financial Services: 830.792.7303 – FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions: 830.792.7217 – admissions@schreiner.edu ANONYMOUS REPORTING Campus Conduct Hotline: 866-943-5787 Page load link Search Schreiner Resources Academic Programs Financial Services University Directory Students | Faculty | Staff Schreiner One Canvas Pounce This site uses cookies and other third-party services. For more information please see our Privacy Policy . Accept & Close Go to Top"
