d work as university team member. Ability to travel overnight with team. Knows and abides by policies of Schreiner University, SCAC, NCAA. Ability to become certified in CPR, First Aid and AED (automatic external defibrillator) Updated annually. Valid Coaching license preferred Must have a valid Texas driver’s license, related insurance, and good driving record. Be willing to obtain a CDL if requested. WORKING CONDITIONS Out of town overnight travel for inter-collegiate athletic contests, meetings, conferences and recruiting efforts using personal vehicle or university vehicle. Weekend and holiday work schedule when necessary. Overtime work required during season and post season play/recruiting/meetings. 75% walking or standing during season and practice. 80% of time at desk during off season. Driving of university vans to transport athletes to games. Apply for Job Schreiner University 2100 Memorial Blvd Kerrville, TX 78028 Directions | 830.896.5411 Financial Services | 830.792.7303 FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions | 830.792.7217 admissions@schreiner.edu Office Hours: 8am – 5pm, Mon -Fri Prospective Students Request Information Apply Financial Services Transcript Requests FAQ Consumer Information Directory About Visitors Donor Alumni Careers at Schreiner Graduate Assistantship Campus Map Schreiner Experiences Box Office Library & Textbooks Schreiner Technology Schreiner Retail Store Community Supporters SU2030 Strategic Plan Security Title IX Privacy Policy CARES Act and HEERF © Schreiner University | 2100 Memorial Blvd. Kerrville, TX 78028-5611 – 830.896.5411 Financial Services: 830.792.7303 – FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions: 830.792.7217 – admissions@schreiner.edu ANONYMOUS REPORTING Campus Conduct Hotline: 866-943-5787 Page load link Search Schreiner Resources Academic Programs Financial Services University Directory Students | Faculty | Staff Schreiner One Canvas Pounce This site uses cookies and other third-party services. For more informat