    "https://schreiner.edu/job/adjunct-chemistry-instructor/": {
      "title": "Adjunct Chemistry Instructor",
      "description": "Adjunct Chemistry Instructor - Schreiner University Skip to content Request Information Anonymous Reporting Toggle Navigation Library Calendar Map Visit Canvas Schreiner One IT Support Academy Prep Shop Toggle Navigation Admissions Academics Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni News Search Apply Now Toggle Navigation Admissions Academic Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni Visit Us Apply Now Shop Schreiner Quick Links News Library Event Calendar Campus Map Schreiner One Canvas Adjunct Chemistry Instructor Adjunct Opportunities Kerrville Texas Posted 8 months ago Website Schreiner University The Department of Chemistry at Schreiner University seeks qualified part-time Adjunct Instructor of Chemistry to teach Introductory Chemistry lecture and/or General Chemistry I and II lecture. Duties include facilitating Introductory Chemistry, or General Chemistry I or General Chemistry 2 lecture (material delivery and assessment of student learning). Online modalities are an option with prior experience. Preference will be given to the applicant with a master’s  degree in chemistry, biochemistry, or chemical engineering, but bachelor’s degrees in science where the coursework included undergraduate credit in General Chemistry I and II will be considered. SUMMARY OF RE S P ONSIBILITI E S Teaches upto 2 chemistry lectures (1 lecture = 3hr load) in the Fall or Spring semester (15wks), with the option of 2 chemistry lectures each summer session (5wks). ESS E NTI A L FUNCT I ONS Teaches Introductory or General I or General II Chemistry lectures Effective content delivery Assessment of student learning Facilitate the above course in online modalities, if applicable. Work with the Chemistry faculty to ensure a quality program OTH E R F U NCTIONS Contribute to team effort by accomplishing related results as needed. Acts to facilitate good communications between employees, clients, and management through interpersonal and professional communication techniques. Maintain University safety rules. Attends division/department meetings as needed and University staff meetings as required. Other duties as assigned. EDU C ATION, EXP E R I ENCE AND SKILLS R E QUI R ED Bachelor’s degree in Chemistry, Biochemistry, Biology, Environmental Health, Environmental Science or Engineering or related field, Masters preferred. Must have a valid Texas driver’s license, related insurance and good driving record Apply for Job Schreiner University 2100 Memorial Blvd Kerrville, TX 78028 Directions | 830.896.5411 Financial Services | 830.792.7303 FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions | 830.792.7217 admissions@schreiner.edu Office Hours: 8am – 5pm, Mon -Fri Prospective Students Request Information Apply Financial Services Transcript Requests FAQ Consumer Information Directory About Visitors Donor Alumni Careers at Schreiner Graduate Assistantship Campus Map Schreiner Experiences Box Office Library & Textbooks Schreiner Technology Schreiner Retail Store Community Supporters SU2030 Strategic Plan Security Title IX Privacy Policy CARES Act and HEERF © Schreiner University | 2100 Memorial Blvd. Kerrville, TX 78028-5611 – 830.896.5411 Financial Services: 830.792.7303 – FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions: 830.792.7217 – admissions@schreiner.edu ANONYMOUS REPORTING Campus Conduct Hotline: 866-943-5787 Page load link Search Schreiner Resources Academic Programs Financial Services University Directory Students | Faculty | Staff Schreiner One Canvas Pounce This site uses cookies and other third-party services. For more information please see our Privacy Policy . Accept & Close Go to Top"
