    "https://schreiner.edu/job/adjunct-instructor-of-computer-science/": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Computer Science",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor of Computer Science - Schreiner University Skip to content Request Information Anonymous Reporting Toggle Navigation Library Calendar Map Visit Canvas Schreiner One IT Support Academy Prep Shop Toggle Navigation Admissions Academics Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni News Search Apply Now Toggle Navigation Admissions Academic Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni Visit Us Apply Now Shop Schreiner Quick Links News Library Event Calendar Campus Map Schreiner One Canvas Adjunct Instructor of Computer Science Full Time Kerrville Texas Posted 11 months ago Website schreineru Schreiner University The Department of Computer Science at Schreiner University seeks qualified individuals to serve as Adjunct Instructors for undergraduate classes including, but not limited to: Teach introductory or advanced Computer Science courses in areas aligned with departmental needs and instructor expertise. Prepare and deliver course content that supports program learning goals and SACSCOC and ABET expectations , including clear syllabi, assignments, assessments, and grading. Evaluate and document Student Learning Outcomes (SLOs) each semester using department-provided rubrics and reporting templates. Participate in the department’s continuous improvement process , including contributing SLO data, assessment commentary, and evidence of student achievement required for ABET preparation. Provide timely, constructive feedback to students and maintain regular communication throughout the semester. Maintain accurate grade records and meet all university deadlines and academic policies. Perform other instructional duties as assigned to support program quality and student success. MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS (EDUCATION, KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, ABILITIES, and EXPERIENCE) Master’s degree or higher in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Software Engineering, Information Systems, or a closely related field, with at least 18 graduate hours in computing disciplines. Demonstrated ability to teach at the undergraduate level; prior college-level teaching experience preferred. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Ability to work effectively with a diverse student population at an MSI/HSI institution. Familiarity with learning outcomes assessment and willingness to contribute to ABET documentation and continuous improvement. In addition to the online application, applicants should submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts, teaching philosophy, the names, addresses and telephone numbers of three references, and other support materials such as teaching evaluations. These can be attached as part of the online application or can be submitted electronically to HRTeam@schreiner.edu if unable to attach to the online application.  Materials that cannot be submitted electronically may be mailed to:  Schreiner University Human Resources Office 2100 Memorial Blvd CMB 6233, Kerrville, Texas 78028. Apply for Job Schreiner University 2100 Memorial Blvd Kerrville, TX 78028 Directions | 830.896.5411 Financial Services | 830.792.7303 FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions | 830.792.7217 admissions@schreiner.edu Office Hours: 8am – 5pm, Mon -Fri Prospective Students Request Information Apply Financial Services Transcript Requests FAQ Consumer Information Directory About Visitors Donor Alumni Careers at Schreiner Graduate Assistantship Campus Map Schreiner Experiences Box Office Library & Textbooks Schreiner Technology Schreiner Retail Store Community Supporters SU2030 Strategic Plan Security Title IX Privacy Policy CARES Act and HEERF © Schreiner University | 2100 Memorial Blvd. Kerrville, TX 78028-5611 – 830.896.5411 Financial Services: 830.792.7303 – FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions: 830.792.7217 – admissions@schreiner.edu ANONYMOUS REPORTING Campus Conduct Hotline: 866-943-5787 Page load link Search Schreiner Resources Academic Programs Financial Services University Directory Students | Faculty | Staff Schreiner One Canvas Pounce This site uses cookies and other third-party services. For more information please see our Privacy Policy . Accept & Close Go to Top"
