    "https://schreiner.edu/job/graduate-assistant-for-the-department-of-history-and-regional-studies/": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant for the Department of History and Regional Studies",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant for the Department of History and Regional Studies Skip to content Request Information Anonymous Reporting Toggle Navigation Library Calendar Map Visit Canvas Schreiner One IT Support Academy Prep Shop Toggle Navigation Admissions Academics Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni News Search Apply Now Toggle Navigation Admissions Academic Campus Life Athletics About Giving Alumni Visit Us Apply Now Shop Schreiner Quick Links News Library Event Calendar Campus Map Schreiner One Canvas Graduate Assistant for the Department of History and Regional Studies Graduate Assistantship Kerrville Texas Posted 1 year ago Website schreineru Schreiner University SUMMARY OF RESPONSIBILITIES The Department of History and Regional Studies seeks a graduate assistant who is willing to work hard to help teach and administer lower-division courses as well as promote the department to prospective students. The graduate assistant will gain experience as a college-level instructor by leading in-class discussions, giving lectures, and grading. They will help the department chair articulate and market the benefits of majoring in History at Schreiner University. Finally, they will help the department facilitate undergraduate research among History majors. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Grade course assignments (attendance, short essays, exams) for two (2) lower-division History courses per semester Attend at least half of the class meetings for two face-to-face lower-division History courses per semester Lead three (3) class discussions in two face-to-face lower-division History course, for a total of six (6) class discussion leads Deliver two (2) lectures per semester in two face-to-face lower-division History course, for a total of four (4) lectures Maintain the database of History majors Assist students in History courses with content-related questions and writing development Promote undergraduate research in History in various ways: encourage History majors to present their work at Schreiner’s annual Academic Showcase find and distribute information to History majors about undergraduate research conferences in the region assist the department chair in the founding of an undergraduate presentation conference at Schreiner University, prospectively called the Hill Country History Conference , “HC²” help History graduates find and pursue publication venues for their senior theses Promote the department in various ways: maintain the department’s table/booth at SU Saturdays, passing out promotional materials and engaging interested students and their parents in the major assist department faculty when they deliver mock classes as SU Saturdays: passing out flyers, keeping attendance, recording contact information of those in attendance develop a database of prospective students develop and maintain an alumni network of History graduates maintain and update the department website assist the department chair to develop a promotional video for the department promote the department through social media (e.g. Instagram) work alongside the department chair to brainstorm promotional ideas, such as virtually promoting the major to high schools and community colleges EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE AND SKILLS REQUIRED Education: Bachelor’s degree, preferably in the Humanities Personable, conversational, with a willingness to talk to prospective students and their parents A willingness and ease with working with undergraduate students Some ability to formulate and deliver lesson plans Some ability to lead class discussions Adequate computer skills Adeptness with the use of Microsoft products: Word, Excel, PowerPoint Familiarity with online learning platforms, e.g. Canvas Familiarity with the use of social media platforms, e.g. Instagram Apply for Job Schreiner University 2100 Memorial Blvd Kerrville, TX 78028 Directions | 830.896.5411 Financial Services | 830.792.7303 FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions | 830.792.7217 admissions@schreiner.edu Office Hours: 8am – 5pm, Mon -Fri Prospective Students Request Information Apply Financial Services Transcript Requests FAQ Consumer Information Directory About Visitors Donor Alumni Careers at Schreiner Graduate Assistantship Campus Map Schreiner Experiences Box Office Library & Textbooks Schreiner Technology Schreiner Retail Store Community Supporters SU2030 Strategic Plan Security Title IX Privacy Policy CARES Act and HEERF © Schreiner University | 2100 Memorial Blvd. Kerrville, TX 78028-5611 – 830.896.5411 Financial Services: 830.792.7303 – FinancialServices@schreiner.edu Admissions: 830.792.7217 – admissions@schreiner.edu ANONYMOUS REPORTING Campus Conduct Hotline: 866-943-5787 Page load link Search Schreiner Resources Academic Programs Financial Services University Directory Students | Faculty | Staff Schreiner One Canvas Pounce This site uses cookies and other third-party services. For more information please see our Privacy Policy . Accept & Close Go to Top"
